---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import Crumbs from "../components/Crumbs.astro";
import RelatedLinks from "../components/RelatedLinks.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: SITE.url + "/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Services", item: SITE.url + "/services" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Conversational analytics", item: SITE.url + "/conversational-analytics" },
    ],
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Conversational analytics on a model | Alluvium"
  description="Someone asks a question in ordinary language and gets the number from a report people already trust. This is not a new chatbot."
  canonicalPath="/conversational-analytics"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article>
    <header class="hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <Crumbs crumbs={[{ href: "/", label: "Home" }, { href: "/services", label: "Services" }, { label: "Conversational analytics" }]} />
        <p class="kicker">Conversational analytics</p>
        <h1>Ask the Power BI reports you already have</h1>
        <p class="lede">Someone asks a question in ordinary language and gets the number from a report people already trust. This is not a new chatbot.</p>
        <p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a Session</a></p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap prose">
        <h2>A chatbot on a pile of spreadsheets will talk. It will not agree with the meeting.</h2>
        <p>The demo answers from whichever file was uploaded last. It does not use one definition of revenue, margin, inventory, or cash.</p>
        <p>Here the question goes to the Power BI reports you already have. The answer is the same number that report would have shown.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band band-alt">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>The question hits the report</h2>
        <p>It does not land on the spreadsheet pile.</p>
        <figure>
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 680 330" role="img" aria-label="A stack of spreadsheets on the left. A question mark points at one bar in a report on the right.">
        <rect x="20" y="108" width="184" height="196" rx="3" fill="#f4f7fa" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="20" y="108" width="184" height="22" fill="#e7f1f8"/>
        <rect x="40" y="124" width="184" height="196" rx="3" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="40" y="124" width="184" height="22" fill="#f4f7fa"/>
        <rect x="60" y="140" width="184" height="176" rx="3" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1c1c1c" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="60" y="140" width="184" height="26" fill="#e7f1f8"/>
        <path d="M88 166 V300 M116 166 V300 M144 166 V300 M172 166 V300 M200 166 V300 M228 166 V300" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="1.5"/>
        <path d="M76 186 H228 M76 210 H228 M76 234 H228 M76 258 H228 M76 282 H228" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="1.5"/>

        <rect x="330" y="136" width="322" height="176" rx="6" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#1c1c1c" stroke-width="2.5"/>
        <line x1="352" y1="276" x2="630" y2="276" stroke="#dcdcdc" stroke-width="2"/>
        <rect x="368" y="224" width="28" height="52" fill="#dcdcdc"/>
        <rect x="416" y="196" width="28" height="80" fill="#397fb0"/>
        <rect x="464" y="156" width="28" height="120" fill="#1c1c1c"/>
        <rect x="512" y="208" width="28" height="68" fill="#397fb0" opacity="0.75"/>
        <rect x="560" y="184" width="28" height="92" fill="#397fb0"/>
        <path d="M446 88 L478 134 L510 88 Z" fill="#ffffff"/>
        <path d="M446 88 L478 134 L510 88" fill="none" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <rect x="400" y="4" width="156" height="88" rx="22" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="2.5"/>
        <path d="M460 42 c0 -14 36 -16 36 0 c0 12 -16 14 -18 26" fill="none" stroke="#397fb0" stroke-width="3.5" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        <circle cx="478" cy="76" r="3.4" fill="#397fb0"/>
        <rect x="442" y="82" width="72" height="14" fill="#ffffff"/>
      </svg>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap prose">
        <h2>What has to be true first</h2>
        <p>The report has to be one people already trust. One definition of the number, refresh in time for the meeting, and people see only the rows they should see. Someone inside the company can change a definition without a fight. If that is not true yet, the questions wait.</p>
        <h2>The answer comes from the report</h2>
        <p>You, or your analysts, ask in plain language. The answer is calculated from the Power BI model behind those reports, using the same definitions the meeting already uses.</p>
        <p>You are asking the reports you have. You are not standing up a separate product with its own data.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <RelatedLinks
      services={[
        { href: "/power-bi-model-health", label: "Power BI model health" },
        { href: "/power-bi-dashboard-optimization-ai-insights", label: "Dashboard optimization" },
        { href: "/analytics-ai-strategy-roadmap", label: "Analytics strategy roadmap" },
      ]}
      posts={[
        { href: "/blog/conversational-analytics-needs-a-trusted-model", label: "Conversational analytics needs a trusted model" },
        { href: "/blog/ask-the-model-dont-screenshot", label: "Ask the model, don’t screenshot" },
        { href: "/blog/semantic-model-is-the-product", label: "The semantic model is the product" },
      ]}
    />
    <CtaBand heading="Bring one report people already trust." text="Book a session. We will pick that report and the questions it should answer." />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
